A||||3||Ed||'88 with deck hump||||1||
Z||000000||Ed||04-16-2001||11:19 PM||||A friend bought an '88 four banger.  The rear deck lid has a hump and a wing.  Did four-cylinder '88's have the humped deck? Or do you think someone may have put on a humped deck to get the wing? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||V8Fiero||04-16-2001||11:47 PM||||If Im not mistaken I think 84 was the only yr that "didnt" have the hump. This was to allow addtional room for the V6 plenum...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-16-2001||11:55 PM||||The hump was to provide space above the engine to aid in airflow/cooling. The side covers in 84 were solid with the grate in the middle. 85 and up (all notchbacks) had the hump for space in the middle and the side covers were grates for cooling. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||04-17-2001||12:17 AM||||OK, thanks for the info.||||reg||1
